=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the cache-then-network data port, also Microsoft.UI-free),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view).
  Namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Battery. The surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by
  route name ("ProjectedRange"), which RouteTable.cs already maps to the /projected-range nav item AND the
  hidden /analytics/range deep-link alias.
- Data source (web useQuery(['range-projection', vehicleId]) · GET /analytics/range-projection?vehicle_id=…):
  ported as the Microsoft.UI-free IRangeProjectionSource. The repository-backed RangeProjectionSource resolves
  the scoped/primary vehicle via the shared IWidgetVehicleSource (native useSelectedVehicle), then runs one
  cache-then-network read of the generated operation get_api_v1_analytics_range_projection (added as
  Operations.Analytics.RangeProjection, validated by OperationsResolveTests) through the shared
  CacheThenNetworkEngine (cacheKey analytics:range-projection:{id}), and parses each emission into the full
  RangeProjection (10 scalars + factors[] + projection_curve[] + scenarios[] + efficiency_matrix[]) via
  RangeProjectionResultMapper. The parameterless ProjectedRangePage() defaults to EmptyRangeProjectionSource
  (renders the empty state) — the established W7 default-feed pattern — while ProjectedRangePage(source,
  localizer) drives the full loading/empty/error/success matrix for DI hosts and the headless tests. No HTTP
  touches the view.
- Interactive "what if": the two web slider useState(80)/useState(20) + the useMemo(interpolateRange) become
  ProjectedRangePageViewModel.WhatIfSpeedKmh/WhatIfTempC (km/h, °C) which re-project the current snapshot in
  place; RangeProjectionProjection.InterpolateRange is the 1:1 port of the web interpolateRange (matrix-bucket
  lookup → heuristic Wh/km fallback → range = capacity·SoC/eff). The view binds two TsSliders to those.
- Units: the endpoint delivers km / km/h / Wh / °C / Wh-per-km. SI display restatement happens only at
  projection time via the shared C# behavior port — UnitFormatters.FormatDistance(km·1000) /
  FormatSpeed(km/h ÷ 3.6) / FormatTemperature(°C) / FormatEnergy(Wh) + ScalarFormatters.FormatPercentage /
  FormatNumber (P1/S5). Nothing non-SI is stored or computed; only the (intrinsically metric) what-if slider
  domains and the .resw "at {0} km/h, {1}°C" template stay km/h/°C, matching the web sliders' hardcoded labels.
- Catalog: all 27 of the page's i18n keys already existed verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw
  (translation.range.*). No catalog rows were added; every visible literal resolves through ILocalizer with
  the web key names (incidental sub-keys range.bucket.* / range.drives / range.factor.* fall back to the web's
  own capitalize-raw / literal behavior when absent, exactly as the web source does).
- AIRangePrediction (the web page's opt-in Helix panel, strings range.aiPredict.*) is a SEPARATE parity unit
  with its own string group — it is not among this unit's 14 panels or 27 strings and is out of scope here.
- Pre-existing blocker fixed: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs had a malformed page-factory
  block (the "YearReview" registration lambda was never closed; the "AutomationList" registration had been
  nested inside it), left red by the prior AutomationListPage runner. That C# syntax error broke MarkupCompile
  Pass1 and cascaded into a WMC9999 XAML-compiler crash on every XAML file. It is the section this prompt must
  edit to register the page, so it was repaired (YearReview lambda closed + un-nested) alongside adding the
  ProjectedRange registration. With it fixed (and one CS0649/3×CA1822 in this prompt's own new files), the full
  solution XAML+C# build is green again.

